	"title"			"ToT Victory Forecaster"
	"description"		"Know who is about to win, and why.

ToT Victory Forecaster annotates the Victories screen with the number the game never shows you: what the Point Goal is about to become, and who already clears it.

[h3]What it does[/h3]
[list]
[*] A civ's score turns [b]red[/b] once it already clears the goal the [i]next[/i] victory tier will set — that civ starts a victory countdown the moment the Point Goal drops.
[*] Hovering a victory column adds, to each tier section of the tooltip, the Point Goal that tier produces and the arithmetic behind it — for example [i]Point Goal 240 = x1.5 of 2nd place 160[/i].
[*] When a countdown is imminent the tooltip names the civ and the Age Progress percentage at which it starts.
[/list]

[h3]Why it matters[/h3]
The Point Goal for a Cultural, Economic or Military victory is a multiple of the [b]second[/b] place score, and that multiple steps down as the Age advances: 2x, then 1.5x, then 1.25x. The goal therefore falls without anyone scoring a single point, and a rival who looks comfortably behind can be one threshold away from a countdown. This mod shows you that threshold before it arrives, and shows the working so you can check it.

[h3]Exact, not predicted[/h3]
[list]
[*] Every figure is arithmetic on current standings. No projections, no score-rate estimates, no guesses.
[*] The victory tier ladder is read live from the game database, so rules mods and future patches are picked up automatically.
[*] The goal shown for the tier in force is cross-checked against the game's own Point Goal, so an error would be visible on the first hover.
[/list]

[h3]Safe and lightweight[/h3]
[list]
[*] UI only. It reads game state and never changes the rules.
[*] Does not affect saved games, and is safe to add to or remove from an existing save at any time.
[*] Civs you have not met stay anonymised, exactly as the base screen presents them.
[*] Adds no panel and no button. It annotates what the screen already draws.
[/list]

Currently English only. Built against Civilization VII build 1.4.0. Open source — feedback welcome."
	"changenote"		"Initial release"
